# Task W (agy): native Wi-Fi acceptance on branch wt/wifi
Worktree: /Users/bagas/Downloads/vphone-wt-wifi (branch wt/wifi). Report id: W-wifi-native.

## Background
wt/wifi (4 Codex commits up to 46aa62a) emulates a BCM43342 FullMAC USB Wi-Fi on the HSIC/EHCI1 port with slirp networking (backend/wifi_dongle.c, wifi_protocol.h, host_wifi.py; README section "Optional BCM43342 HSIC Wi-Fi"). Synthetic contracts pass (`backend/wifi_contract_test.py`), but the native iOS boot acceptance has never been run.

## Step 1: bring the branch up to date
`git merge agx-meta-hle` (that branch is the main integration branch, now at e63a591). Expect conflicts in backend/live_run.py and backend/display_probe.py: keep BOTH the `--wifi` option and the new virtual-activated default + MTTCG default of live_run.py. Rebuild QEMU here, run `backend/wifi_contract_test.py`, `backend/ehci_contract_test.py` and `.venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -s tests`. Commit the merge.

## Step 2: native acceptance (virtual-activated profile, Cocoa window, `-d unimp` / qemu-trace)
Verify, in order, each with evidence:
1. HSIC enumeration: device 0a5c:4334, TRX download (length/CRC ok), DL_GO, re-enumeration as 0a5c:bd21.
2. AppleBCMWLAN driver attaches (serial/kernel log), without the old ~22 s HSIC retry loop.
3. A scan returns the synthetic AP whose SSID is the host SSID (or `VPHONE_WIFI_SSID`).
4. Join/association succeeds.
5. DHCP lease: use a QEMU `-object filter-dump,id=f0,netdev=wifi0,file=<out>/wifi.pcap` and show DISCOVER/OFFER/REQUEST/ACK; optionally show guest traffic (DNS) afterwards.
6. If reachable: unlock (scripted swipe) and open Settings -> Wi-Fi with taps to show the network connected (screenshot).
Fix model bugs you find on wt/wifi (keep Wi-Fi absent when --wifi is not given).

## Done when
Report with PASS/FAIL per stage 1-6 and evidence paths, contracts/tests passing, commits on wt/wifi.
## Common rules (all workers)
- Read CLAUDE_HANDOVER.md sections 20-23 first (and backend/README.md for tooling). The project emulates an iPhone 5s (A7, iOS 7) in a patched QEMU (`backend/s5l8960x.c`).
- Work ONLY in your own worktree and commit only to your own branch. Do not touch /Users/bagas/Downloads/vphone-legacy (main checkout) or any other worktree, do not merge into other branches, do not push.
- `build/` is a symlink to the shared image store: never write into it. The default profile is `build/virtual-activated-profile-v5/` (plan `boot/boot_plan.json`, `system.raw`, `data.raw`); `backend/live_run.py` uses it by default with MTTCG and always clones images. For timed probes use `backend/display_probe.py` with `--plan/--diagnostic-system/--diagnostic-data` pointing at those files and a fresh `--output` under your worktree.
- Build your own QEMU in this worktree: `backend/.venv/bin/python scripts/qemu/build_backend.py` (writes backend/bin/qemu-system-aarch64 here). Rebuild once before blaming a regression; compare `AGX replay target` vs `AGX RT queue` counts in qemu-trace.log.
- Every QEMU launch must show the Cocoa window: `VPHONE_DISPLAY=cocoa` for display_probe.py; live_run.py always does.
- Delete disposable image clones (`<output>/images`, ~3 GB) after each probe. Keep evidence small (logs, PNGs, json).
- macOS mediaanalysisd sometimes loads the CPU; wait for `uptime` load < 5 before timing measurements. Other workers run QEMU in parallel; keep at most one QEMU of your own running at a time.
- Lock screen timing on this profile: "slide to unlock" around 90 s guest; the display idles off ~30 s after content appears (touches are ignored while dark). Working scripted unlock: `VPHONE_TOUCH_SCRIPT='at=95;down 40,1036;hold 0.3;move 600,1036 dur=3 steps=180;hold 1.0;up'`.
- No guest-binary patching unless your task says so. Fix things in the emulator/board model.
- Write your report to `research/reports/<task-id>.md` (what you found, what changed, evidence paths, PASS/FAIL per goal, what is still open) and commit code + report with a clear message ending in a `Co-Authored-By:` line for yourself. Do not claim success without evidence.
